// REQUIRES: uv
// RUN: zkc-opt %pir-seal-full %pir-project-full %S/../Encoding/chaum-pedersen.mlir > %t.mlir
// RUN: zkc-run %t.mlir --vectors %S/Inputs/chaum-pedersen-exec-vectors.json | FileCheck %s
//
// Execution parity for the Chaum-Pedersen (DLEQ) twin: two
// commitments, one challenge, one response replayed bit-exactly
// against the oracle-generated golden vectors. The
// mismatched_statement vector is the protocol's point: the same
// honest transcript against a second statement leg that is NOT h^x
// dies at verify2 — the two checks bind one exponent across both
// groups. The committed vector file is the cross-implementation
// execution contract; the uv-gated lines below regenerate it from
// the oracle and require byte identity.
//
// RUN: %uv python -m oracle.exec chaum-pedersen > %t.vectors
// RUN: diff %t.vectors %S/Inputs/chaum-pedersen-exec-vectors.json
//
// CHECK: honest: accept [1956989731398489217]
// CHECK-NEXT: tampered_response: check_failure [1956989731398489217]
// CHECK-NEXT: mismatched_statement: check_failure [1061406300520161278]
// CHECK-NEXT: trailing_byte: proof_trailing_data [1956989731398489217]
// CHECK-NEXT: truncated: abi_decode_failure [1956989731398489217]
// CHECK-NEXT: noncanonical_value: abi_decode_failure []
